Carotenoid microcapsules are micro‑encapsulated forms of active carotenoids such as beta‑carotene, lutein, lycopene, astaxanthin and related compounds. They are produced through spray‑drying, emulsion solidification, complex coacervation or liposome techniques. Encapsulation shields the pigments from light, oxygen and heat while improving dispersibility and bioavailability in food matrices, feed rations and dietary‑supplement formulations. The products are typically supplied as powders or water‑dispersible beadlets and serve as natural colourants or nutritional fortification agents.
